1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,521
The Birds: when the skies darken, pure animal terror follows.

2
00:00:03,741 --> 00:00:05,427
Here's how this vignette plays.

3
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:09,913
There's no Killer board: put the Bloodlust and Bird Spawn cards next to the

4
00:00:09,913 --> 00:00:11,631
Location, and start Horror at four.

5
00:00:11,851 --> 00:00:16,137
Put a three-Bird token on the Killer's start space, then one Bird on every empty

6
00:00:16,137 --> 00:00:16,459
space.

7
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:21,576
To win, save all the Special Victims: one, two or three, depending on difficulty.

8
00:00:21,796 --> 00:00:25,908
They come out when you unlock your Ultimate Ability or no normal Victims are left.

9
00:00:25,908 --> 00:00:28,516
You lose if every space has three Birds, or you die.

10
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:31,787
Birds are Minions, and they never move on their own.

11
00:00:32,007 --> 00:00:36,261
To spawn, roll two dice and choose which one sets how many and which sets where,

12
00:00:36,261 --> 00:00:39,559
using the Bird Spawn card. Full spaces overflow to neighbours.

13
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:44,951
Birds attack in your space and in every space with three Birds, one target each, for

14
00:00:44,951 --> 00:00:47,897
damage equal to the number of Birds. Victims go first.

15
00:00:48,117 --> 00:00:52,265
Your Reactions can protect anyone in your space, and each damage you deal removes

16
00:00:52,265 --> 00:00:52,725
one Bird.

17
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:57,794
A few tips. Birds spread rather than chase, so race for the exits and only kill them

18
00:00:57,794 --> 00:00:58,504
when you must.

19
00:00:58,724 --> 00:01:03,282
Melanie's Ultimate removes Birds cheaply, and small boards like Storybook Woods fill

20
00:01:03,282 --> 00:01:04,313
up fast. Good luck.

